  "post": {
    "caption": "Abraham Lincoln married Mary Todd in Springfield, Illinois, on November 4, 1842, at her sister's home. Lincoln went to see Reverend Charles Dresser that morning and the wedding took place that evening. Tradition says he bought the plain gold ring at Chatterton's jewelry shop, it was engraved inside with Love is Eternal, and Mary wore it for about forty years.",
